# Rust build artifacts
/target/

# IDE/editor
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Generated by cargo
**/*.rs.bk

# Python virtual env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ScyllaHide binaries (user-downloaded, do not commit)
HookLibrary*.dll
InjectorCLI*.exe

# Local toolchain wiring.  `.cargo/config.toml` points the i686 linker at an
# absolute path under this machine's `D:\Tools`, and documents why a synthetic
# `libgcc_eh.a` is needed.  That is environment state, not source: committing it
# would break every other checkout.  The reasoning lives in AGENTS.md instead.
.cargo/

# Temporary / audit reports
SESSION_REPORT.txt
AUDIT_REPORT.md
_ran.flag*.log
build.bat
.hermes-tmp.*
CLAUDE.md
scylla_hide.ini
# ...except the profile file this project authors and ships as an asset.  The
# bare pattern above matches at any depth, which swallowed it too — the intent
# was only to keep the user-downloaded copy out of the tree.
!crates/cli/assets/scylla_hide.ini
run_unpack.bat
unpack_*.log
